name kixfont
category Package
revision 18488
shortdesc A font for KIX codes.
relocated 1
longdesc The KIX code is a barcode-like format used by the Dutch PTT to
longdesc encode country codes, zip codes and street numbers in a machine-
longdesc readable format. If printed below the address line on bulk
longdesc mailings, a discount can be obtained. The font is distributed
longdesc in Metafont format, and covers the numbers and upper-case
longdesc letters.
